<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jun of Gojoseon</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. ?–194 BCE</span> · Also known as King Jun</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jun was the last king of the Gija line of Gojoseon in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/korea">Korea</a>, according to Chinese and Korean historical tradition. Around 194 BCE he was overthrown by Wiman, a refugee from the Chinese state of Yan whom he had employed to guard his frontier. Jun is said to have fled south by sea to the Jin and Mahan region, where he took the title King of Han.</p></div>
